{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XPpvwAfFDMLGKwtxTaiyGh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: python -m pytest\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting,\n6\tand worth his attention â€” smaller high-trust catalog, closed measurable value loop â€” evolving the\n7\texisting pipeline. Locked-preserved: KB schema (additive migrations only) + browsable library,\n8\tsingle-owner security gate, deterministic cost telemetry (CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml), Helping Hand\n9\tMCP + publisher. Backfills NEVER DELETE (re-kind/retire only; dry-run + audit mandatory). The\n10\tworking tree is production (sweeps 01:07â€“05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends with a clean\n11\tcommitted tree. server.py waves end with plugin rebuild + reinstall (reinstall is MANUAL â€” John\n12\tinstalls the rebuilt `.plugin` in Cowork) + live smoke. No test weakening; the count may only rise.\n13\tOUT: discovery parallelism; issue #5.\n14\t\n15\t> Master plan + evidence (E1â€“E23): `docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md`. Waves run in series.\n16\t> Counts of live-KB rows cited below are 2026-06-09 snapshots and drift nightly â€” every backfill\n17\t> resolves its working set by RULE in its `--dry-run --audit-out` pass, never by these counts.\n18\t\n19\t## Wave 1 â€” De-noised, ranked top finds + honest adoption metric (the felt vertical)\n20\t\n21\t**Intent:** Make the next 06:47 briefing worth reading by changing only the two briefing-side files\n22\t(`morning_briefing.py`, `briefing_delivery.py` â€” neither is executed by the overnight sweeps, so the\n23\tdeploy deadline is 06:47, not 01:07). No DB or pipeline changes in this wave; the briefing-side\n24\tqueries carry their own noise exclusions so they are correct even though tonight's rows are still\n25\tmis-kinded (E3: `upsert_artifact` never