, tested with the env var unset. HH server D1: `kind='model'` excluded from single-mode routing + `_record_surfaced` but kept in ranked/compare paths; D2: papers REMAIN matchable for pull queries, clearly kind-labeled, never auto-loaded. New `bin/noise_audit.py` standing zero-noise check + cross-surface count regression tests.\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Weekly digest v1 + notability signal\n- PRECONDITION: authenticated `gh` CLI (verify before backfill; HALT-AND-ASK John if unauthenticated, since 60 req/hr would stall multi-hour).\n- Schedules the already-built-but-never-run `check_link_health.py` as a weekly task and runs one supervised backfill over ~283 active GitHub-linked artifacts (keyed on `canonical_url LIKE '%github.com%'` since `github_full_name` is never populated), lighting up stars/staleness signals.\n- `weekly_digest.py` + weekly task produces `reports/weekly/<date>.md` (top finds with why-lines + stars, a separated \"papers worth reading\" section, catalog-health deltas), delivered via the existing `briefing_delivery` channel. done-when: â‰¥80% of active GitHub-linked artifacts have `gh_stargazers`.\n\n## Wave 4 â€” The taste score\n- Replaces the interim heuristic with a persisted interestingness score tuned to John's profile, correctly priced/metered (E17 unpriced-tag trap: the priced key and the called tag must be provably identical, asserted by a `test_pricing_keys.py` extension). Scope: new finds + any unscored artifact reaching a serving surface â€” never the full back catalog.\n- Adds migration `0025_interest_score.sql` (additive: `interest_score`, `interest_why`, `interest_scored_at`), `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (versioned, John-editable: Claude/agent ecosystem, usable>academic, novelty over volume), and `roles/taste.py` scorer wired post-librarian with a nightly cap (`AURORA_TASTE_NIGHTLY_CAP` default 40) and heuristic fallback. Ranking surfaces switch to `interest_score`; `interest_why` upgrades the why-lines. The nightly leg is armed but separately verified by John from the next morning's data.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Close the loop\n- Bounded usage modifier in HH `_compute_matches` (post-cosine): per-artifact boost from `loaded` / decay from `dismissed`, bounded Â±0.10 with 30-day-half-life exponential decay (both decided), applied identically in top_finds + digest ranking on top of interest_score â€” the unbounded-feedback trap is explicitly guarded.\n- Retirement policy (`bin/retirement_policy.py`, nightly, audited, reversible): N=2 consecutive stale probes â†’ retire; never-surfaced AND `interest_score < 0.3` AND older than 60 days â†’ retire (env-overridable defaults). Acceptance is fixture-based; the live stale-retirement leg is armed, not demonstrated (needs ~2 weeks of probe history).\n- Digest gains a value section: suggestion-adoption trend, loads/dismissals, and profile-drift hints that prompt a manual `INTEREST_PROFILE.md` edit with NO auto-mutation.\n\nWant me to save this as a memory or write it to a file?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8033,"cache_read_input_tokens":32896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8033},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbce36b1-c2d9-4f04-90cf-d6549f3c4701","uuid":"2e70b29d-dfaf-4475-a7ff-8444f7844565","request_id":"req_011CcKGye9VLZVujmyvpJLMQ"}
